### GET request to token bucket test endpoint without rate limiter (bypasses the gateway route entirely)
GET http://localhost:8083/test/tokenbucket

### GET request to leaky bucket test endpoint without rate limiter (bypasses the gateway route entirely)
GET http://localhost:8083/test/leakybucket

### GET health check
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health

### GET registered routes from the gateway
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/gateway/routes


### =========================================================
### Token Bucket (route1): /tokenbucket/** -> StripPrefix -> sample-api /user
### capacity=5, refill 5 tokens / 60s -> 6th call within the window should 429
### =========================================================
GET http://localhost:8083/tokenbucket/user


### =========================================================
### Leaky Bucket (route2): /leakybucket/** -> StripPrefix -> sample-api /login
### capacity=10, leak 1/sec -> 11th call in quick succession should 429
### =========================================================
GET http://localhost:8083/leakybucket/login


### =========================================================
### Sliding Window Counter, in-memory (slidingwindow): /slidingwindow/** -> StripPrefix -> sample-api /user
### limit=3 requests / 30s window, scoped per client IP for the whole route (same as route1/route2)
### =========================================================
GET http://localhost:8083/slidingwindow/user


### =========================================================
### Sliding Window Counter, Redis-backed (slidingwindow-redis): /slidingwindow-redis/** -> StripPrefix -> sample-api /user
### limit=3 requests / 30s window, scoped per client IP for the whole route, state lives in Redis (survives app restarts)
### =========================================================
GET http://localhost:8083/slidingwindow-redis/user


### =========================================================
### Path + User-ID keyed (userpath-demo): /userpath-demo/** -> StripPrefix -> sample-api /user or /login
### keyBy: PATH,USER_ID -> quota is independent per (downstream path, X-User-Id) pair
### capacity=3, refill 3 tokens / 60s -> 4th call for the same path+user should 429
### =========================================================

### alice on /userpath-demo/user (allowed, 1 of 3)
GET http://localhost:8083/userpath-demo/user
X-User-Id: alice

### bob on the SAME path /userpath-demo/user (allowed - independent quota per user)
GET http://localhost:8083/userpath-demo/user
X-User-Id: bob

### alice on a DIFFERENT path /userpath-demo/login (allowed - independent quota per path)
GET http://localhost:8083/userpath-demo/login
X-User-Id: alice

### no X-User-Id header (falls back to the shared "anonymous" bucket for this path)
GET http://localhost:8083/userpath-demo/user